{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"world war one\" (+ deaths casualties fatalities) (+ \"lesson plan\" worksheet \"teaching resource\") (+ graph statistics data))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_01_845890230#0_947615550","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1241","rank":1,"snippet":"Sheet Music Flanders Fields Video Download Lesson Plans Lesson Plans Overview Educational Kit Contents<cover>Lesson Plan Intro Lesson #1-Story Behind Poem Lesson #2-Poem Analysis Lesson #3-Inspiration for Poppy Lesson #4-Story of John McCrae Lesson #5- Story Behind Song Lesson #6-Song Analysis Flanders Fields Poem Bio-John McCrae John McCrae Timeline Bio-Anthony Hutchcroft Song Reviews Contact Info Directory A Brief Outline of WWI WWI Chronology WWI Statistics WW1 Photos Lt Col John McCrae Listen to Audio Files World War One – Statistics The First World War, also known as the “Great War” or the “War to End All Wars,” was global war. Battles were fought in the trenches using machine guns, poisonous gas and tanks Battles were fought at sea and coastal towns were shelled by German warships Planes were used for battle and for positioning and reporting on the enemy Battles were fought by air with many air raids by German Zeppelins Civilian workers produced weapons, munitions, equipment and supplies for the troops Medical personal ministered to the hundreds of thousands of wounded, maimed and sick Allied Countries - Losses: Military Casualties: </cover>5.7 million Civilian Casualties: 3.67 million Military Wounded: 12.8 million Allied "}}
