{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1245"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_39_1546092525#0_3246111601","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1245","rank":2,"snippet":"000000 , \"headings\": \"Battle of Gallipoli Facts Battle of Gallipoli Facts 19 Battle of Gallipoli Facts for Kids Pictures of the Battle of Gallipoli \" , \"segment\": \"19 Battle of Gallipoli Facts for Kids and Students Home War Facts World War 1 Facts Battle of Gallipoli Facts Battle of Gallipoli Facts Battle Name: Battle of Gallipoli Battle Start Date: February 17th, 1915 Battle End Date: January 9th, 1916 Battle Belligerents: Allied Powers and Central Powers Battle Winner: Central Powers Total <cover>Casualties: 500,000+ 19 Battle of Gallipoli Facts for Kids The Battle of Gallipoli was a military campaign during World War 1. </cover>The Battle of Gallipoli is also known as the Gallipoli campaign, the Dardanelles campaign or the Battle of Çanakkale. The Battle of Gallipoli was fought between the Ottoman Empire and The United Kingdom. The Ottoman Empire was supported by the German Empire and Austro-Hungarian Empire (Central Powers).\" , \"start_char\": 0.000000 , \"title\": \"19 Battle of Gallipoli Facts for Kids and Students\" , \"url\": \"https://www.factsjustforkids.com/war-facts/world-war-"}}
