{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_39_1546088573#6_3246110213","relevance":3,"reason":"This is another segment of the same student-facing World War 1 Facts for Kids page already found to include overall military and civilian death estimates; this segment also discusses the Somme as one of the bloodiest battles with over one million casualties.","learned":"The World War 1 Facts for Kids page also highlights major battle casualty scale, including over one million casualties at the Battle of the Somme."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ ww1 \"world war i\" \"first world war\") casualties (+ graph chart visualizing visualization) (+ students lesson classroom))","reason":"Shift toward lesson or classroom resources specifically using graphs/charts/visualization to help students understand the scale of WWI casualties and deaths."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ ww1 \"world war i\" \"first world war\") casualties (+ graph chart visualizing visualization) (+ students lesson classroom))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_27_1191729101#11_2394351934","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1247","rank":1,"snippet":"Impact of War GCSE Revision booklet: Weimar and Nazi Germany (31 Pages) Germany 1919-39, Online CPD for teachers. Hitler’s Rise to Power Revision Chart<cover>Lesson: The Role of the SA. Usefulness of Sources Life in Nazi Germany – Revision Chart Rise of Hitler The Rise of the Nazi Party. Themes and Factors. Weimar Germany Lessons and Teachers Resources German History Homepage Weimar Republic Revision Diagrams Revision Diagrams \" , \"segment\": \"Trade was hard to come by as most of her previous trading partners now sunned Germany, preferring to do Business with the victorious Allies. Likewise the Germans struggled diplomatically, most notoriously their views were ignored at the Peace conference at Versailles. Physical cost of the war The cost of the First World War for Germany is estimated to be in the region of $38 Billion. In addition to this consider the massive loss of life. Germany suffered the loss of 1.7 million young men, with another 4.3 million men being wounded during the conflict. The total casualties </cover>amounted to over 7 million, though this includes some men who were prisoners or listed as missing. 20 Classroom Posters £ 5.00 Add to basket Back "}}
