{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_03_1428484762#0_2349416791","relevance":2,"reason":"This is a student-facing Spanish Flu page, not a dedicated World War I deaths resource, but it directly states that 17 million soldiers and civilians were killed during WW1 as a comparison.","learned":"A kids' Spanish Flu page states that Spanish Flu deaths were almost three times the 17 million soldiers and civilians killed during WW1."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ ww1 \"world war 1\" \"world war i\") (+ \"17 million\" \"16 million\" \"20 million\") (+ \"soldiers and civilians\" casualties deaths) (+ facts overview))","reason":"Search for WWI-focused overview/facts pages that directly state the total death toll in millions, likely yielding grade-3 evidence rather than disease pages."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ ww1 \"world war 1\" \"world war i\") (+ \"17 million\" \"16 million\" \"20 million\") (+ \"soldiers and civilians\" casualties deaths) (+ facts overview))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_30_1049289600#3_2317503530","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1249","rank":1,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_30_1049289600#3_2317503530\" , \"end_char\": 1218.000000 , \"headings\": \"15 interesting WW1 and trench warfare facts. 15 interesting WW1 and trench warfare facts.\" , \"segment\": \"WWI is the sixth deadliest conflict in world history. 9. WWI was fought from 1914-1918 on every ocean and on almost every continent. Most of the fighting, however, took place in Europe. 10. WWI was fought from 1914-1918 on every ocean and on almost every continent. Most of the fighting, however, took place in Europe. 11. There were over 35 million civilian and soldier <cover>casualties in WWI. Over 15 million died and 20 million were wounded.\" , \"start_char\": 779.000000 , \"title\": \"Facts - WW1</cover>\" , \"url\": \"https://trenchwarfareinfo.weebly.com/facts.html\" }"}}
